# Cloudflare's Deploy to Cloudflare flow reads `.env.example` and turns this
# assignment into a deploy-time secret prompt. Choose a unique random value of
# 32–512 visible ASCII characters without spaces. It proves that you own the
# deployment when you claim the server, and is deliberately separate from the generated sync token.
# Never reuse the sync token here.
KAOS_CLAIM_SECRET=
#
# For local development, pass overrides directly when needed:
#   npm run dev -- --var KAOS_CLAIM_SECRET:local-claim-secret-at-least-32-chars
# Or use SYNC_TOKEN as an explicit auth override:
#   npm run dev -- --var SYNC_TOKEN:dev-sync-token
#
# Attachments and snapshots stay disabled until you add an R2 binding named
# `KAOS_BUCKET` in the Cloudflare dashboard.
